desc:TwoStorms EQ
tags: eq equalizer
author: TwoStorms
version: 2.0

// A parametric EQ with an Act built in: its output gain, meters, Auto (Target, Match, Reference),
// Drive link and Finale are a TwoStorms Act, so TwoStorms Gain Stage lists and stages it like one.
// Up to 16 bands (bell, shelves, notch, band pass, high and low pass at 6 to 96 dB/oct), each with its
// own frequency, gain and Q, a channel (Stereo, Left, Right, Mid, Side), an optional gain-dependent Q,
// and optional dynamics (compress, or expand like a conventional downward expander; ratio, knee and a peak or RMS detector, from the main
// input or a sidechain on inputs 3-4). The filters are matched to the analog curves up to Nyquist and
// glide when you move a setting. Zero latency by default; optional linear phase, natural phase (the
// analog filters' own phase with a short latency) and lookahead. Auto gain (curve or program-dependent),
// solo per band, delta, input and output gain, dry/wet, A/B sets with level-matched Bypass and Swap,
// a pre/post analyzer and a sidechain view. Set dynamic thresholds listens, then sets every dynamic band's threshold
// so it reaches its range on the loudest moments.
// Needs REAPER 6.74 or newer.
slider1:0<0,3,1{2,4,6,8}>-Channels
slider2:0<0,2,1{Auto,Always,Never}>-Finale (Auto = the last Act in the chain)
slider3:0<0,2,1{Peak,RMS,LUFS}>-Auto measure
slider4:-12<-60,0,0.01>-Auto target
slider5:4<0,7,1{Manual,1 s,2 s,3 s,5 s,10 s,20 s,30 s}>-Auto time
slider6:1<0,1,1{Off,On}>-Link 1-2
slider7:1<0,1,1{Off,On}>-Link 3-4
slider8:1<0,1,1{Off,On}>-Link 5-6
slider9:1<0,1,1{Off,On}>-Link 7-8
